WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.567 --> 00:00:03.203
(slow piano music)

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:14.881
- My job,

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:15.749
I enjoy it very much.

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:17.984
My contribution conservation,

00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:20.387
it's something that make me
proud.

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:23.289
Working with rangers and
patrols,

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:24.624
with guides,

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:26.393
with animal trackers.

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:28.928
This is the best office in the
world.

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:30.730
(slow piano music)

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:33.400
- The growth of the
country and the energy,

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:37.370
it's almost duplicated in any
other sphere of the society,

00:00:37.437 --> 00:00:38.204
so like,

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:39.038
coffee shops,

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:40.206
art centers,

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:42.142
you feel that energy.

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:43.176
The energy,

00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:46.012
the creativity is part of the
whole fabric

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:46.980
of society right now.

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:48.214
It's a vibe.

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:51.017
(slow piano music)

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:52.485
- I'm trying to push the
boundaries

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:54.320
of things which are made in
Rwanda,

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:57.023
taking the inspiration from
what we have traditionally,

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:58.491
but make them more modern.

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:02.162
My inspiration for my designs,

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:04.564
the colorful patterns all over
Rwanda

00:01:04.631 --> 00:01:05.965
and our tradition too.

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:07.400
I love to go in the market

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:09.736
and just watch people
how they combine colors.

00:01:09.803 --> 00:01:10.670
It's beautiful.

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:15.575
- Nyungwe National Park
is a mountain rainforest.

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:18.044
It's a park rich in
biodiversity.

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:20.513
We have 13 species of primates,

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:23.383
more than 300 species of birds

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:26.719
and it's where we have the
fastest source of the Nile.

00:01:26.786 --> 00:01:29.689
There is something special
that we need to protect.

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:32.659
(slow piano music)

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:38.731
- I'm proud of my country
because the resilience

00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:41.267
and willingness to work hard,

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:42.569
to learn from each other.

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:46.239
Together, we'll go further
than if we work individually.

00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:49.108
What's unique about Rwandan
coffee is the altitude,

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:50.777
the environment makes a huge
difference.

00:01:50.844 --> 00:01:54.147
You get that smooth refreshing
taste

00:01:54.214 --> 00:01:55.949
and we have won numerous awards.

00:01:57.183 --> 00:02:01.254
- The past has a big influence
also to how I see Rwanda.

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:02.622
For example I use intore,

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:03.823
the traditional dancers.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:05.391
It's beautiful and it's
graceful.

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:07.894
So that's what I wanted to
explain it in my clothes.

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:10.363
It's graceful but strong at the
same time.

00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:14.567
- There's a word that
we use called agaciro.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:17.003
Agaciro means the idea of self
worth,

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:17.971
self respect.

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:20.073
And it translates in
everything that we do.

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:24.644
- Agaciro means the dignity of
Rwandans,

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:25.845
working together,

00:02:25.912 --> 00:02:27.046
put efforts together.

00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:29.883
It makes me proud to be Rwandan.

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:35.188
- Agaciro for me it's a very
powerful word

00:02:35.255 --> 00:02:36.523
which has so much meaning.

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:37.957
Be grateful,

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:39.292
be respectful,

00:02:39.359 --> 00:02:40.126
be resilient,

00:02:40.193 --> 00:02:41.361
be an example.

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:45.131
- There is a new change,

00:02:45.198 --> 00:02:48.635
there is a new Rwanda being
created and I'm part of it.

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:53.339
- There's an energy that's out
there

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:55.775
welcoming every single
person to come visit Rwanda,

00:02:55.842 --> 00:02:56.609
walk the streets,

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:58.177
talk to the people,

00:02:58.244 --> 00:02:59.846
you'll be amazed what you
discover.

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:04.250
- Rwanda is a land of dream.

